# oomd-drill.slice — a bounded, throwaway slice for reproducibly proving
# systemd-oomd's managed-kill path. NOT a fleet unit; started on demand by
# bin/oomd-drill and torn down after. No [Install], never enabled.
#
# Why this exists: app-pi\x2dissue.slice carries the real 80%/60s kill policy,
# but driving the worker slice to 80% pressure live would throttle real
# workers. This slice isolates the same ManagedOOMMemoryPressure=kill mechanism
# behind a low limit and a hard MemoryMax, so the drill proves oomd fires and
# spares lifelines without stressing the fleet.
#
# MemoryMax=1G bounds the hog: it hits the wall, stalls on allocation, PSI
# memory pressure climbs, oomd kills the hog cgroup after
# DefaultMemoryPressureDurationSec (60s, set in /etc/systemd/oomd.conf.d on the
# host). 5% is a deliberately low trip point so the drill fires fast; the real
# worker slice uses 80% (see app-pi\x2dissue.slice for why).
#
# Scope: this slice only. sshd, tailscaled, fleet-heartbeat and the intake
# timers are NOT under it and stay `auto`, so the drill can never take a
# lifeline — same isolation property the production policy relies on.
[Slice]
ManagedOOMMemoryPressure=kill
ManagedOOMMemoryPressureLimit=5%
MemoryMax=1G
